  Any blessed spellbook can be successfully read.  Intelligence 
can be improved.  Proper armor selection can actually improve 
spell casting ability.  So can practice.

  Valkyries can get to basic in the attack and escape spell 
schools.  The Valk special spell is cone of cold.  

  A lot of spells are "off-line" spells, in that they are better
used when not in combat: light, identify, invisibility, 
levitation, haste self, etc.   The last three are escape spells 
and can be "pumped up" to last longer.  

  Haste self especially can be a (temporary) replacement for 
speed boots.  #jumping can get you past some traps and short 
stretches of water/lava.  Jumping also lets you travel over twice
as fast as speed boots.

  Force bolt and drain life can be useful ranged attacks where 
you don't want to risk throwing Mjollnir.  (Hint: Giant Eels).

  Cone of cold can get you past long stretches of water/lava.

  Magic missile is a level 2 spell that is the perfect ranged 
attack: 
	- Nothing to pick up.
	- No harm to inventory (yours or the monster's).
        - Can hit multiple monsters.
 	- Can be reflected down a passage or off a wall at 
          monsters not in the direct line of fire/sight.
        - does [(XPlvl/2) + 1 ] d6 worth of damage with each hit.
          (The higher your level, the more damage each hit does.)
          - XP level 30 characters average 48 hp worth of damage 
            per hit.  Makes Mjollnir and Grayswandir look sick.


